msgid "If **wait** is true, then returns once **func** has returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:7: ../include/linux/smp.h:84
msgid ""
"You must not call this function with disabled interrupts or from a hardware "
"interrupt handler or from a bottom half handler.  The exception is that it "
"may be used during early boot while early_boot_irqs_disabled is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:7: ../include/linux/smp.h:280
msgid "``smp_processor_id ()``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:7: ../include/linux/smp.h:278
msgid "get the current (stable) CPU id"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:7: ../include/linux/smp.h:279
msgid ""
"This is the normal accessor to the CPU id and should be used whenever "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:7: ../include/linux/smp.h:282
msgid "The CPU id is stable when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:7: ../include/linux/smp.h:284
msgid "IRQs are disabled;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:7: ../include/linux/smp.h:285
msgid "preemption is disabled;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:7: ../include/linux/smp.h:286
msgid "the task is CPU affine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:7: ../include/linux/smp.h:288
msgid ""
"When CONFIG_DEBUG_PREEMPT=y, we verify these assumptions and WARN when "
"smp_processor_id() is used when the CPU id is not stable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:756
msgid "Run a function on a specific CPU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:762 ../kernel/smp.c:777
msgid "``int cpu``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:757
msgid "Specific target CPU for this function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:760 ../kernel/smp.c:1149
msgid "If true, wait until function has completed on other CPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:762 ../kernel/smp.c:791
#: ../kernel/smp.c:826 ../kernel/smp.c:1282
msgid "**Return**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:762
msgid "``0`` on success, else a negative status code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:771
msgid "Run an asynchronous function on a specific CPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:773 ../kernel/smp.c:1276
msgid "The CPU to run on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:775
msgid "``call_single_data_t *csd``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:774
msgid "Pre-allocated and setup data structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:775
msgid ""
"Like smp_call_function_single(), but the call is asynchonous and can thus be "
"done from contexts with disabled interrupts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:778
msgid ""
"The caller passes his own pre-allocated data structure (ie: embedded in an "
"object) and is responsible for synchronizing it such that the IPIs performed "
"on the **csd** are strictly serialized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:782
msgid ""
"If the function is called with one csd which has not yet been processed by "
"previous call to smp_call_function_single_async(), the function will return "
"immediately with -EBUSY showing that the csd object is still in progress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:787
msgid "**NOTE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:788
msgid ""
"Be careful, there is unfortunately no current debugging facility to validate "
"the correctness of this serialization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:791
msgid "``0`` on success or negative errno value on error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:817
msgid "Run a function on any of the given cpus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:818
msgid "The mask of cpus it can run on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:822 ../kernel/smp.c:1033
msgid "``int wait``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:821
msgid "If true, wait until function has completed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:822
msgid "Selection preference:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:823
msgid "current cpu if in **mask**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:824
msgid "nearest cpu in **mask**, based on NUMA topology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:827
msgid "``0`` on success, else a negative status code (if no cpus were online)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1008
msgid "Run a function on a set of CPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1014 ../kernel/smp.c:1037
#: ../kernel/smp.c:1157
msgid ""
"You must not call this function with disabled interrupts or from a hardware "
"interrupt handler or from a bottom half handler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1017
msgid ""
"**func** is not called on the local CPU even if **mask** contains it.  "
"Consider using on_each_cpu_cond_mask() instead if this is not desirable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1029
msgid "Run a function on all other CPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1034
msgid ""
"If **wait** is true, then returns once **func** has returned; otherwise it "
"returns just before the target cpu calls **func**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1137
msgid ""
"Call a function on each processor for which the supplied function cond_func "
"returns true, optionally waiting for all the required CPUs to finish. This "
"may include the local processor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1143
msgid "``smp_cond_func_t cond_func``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1141
msgid ""
"A callback function that is passed a cpu id and the info parameter. The "
"function is called with preemption disabled. The function should return a "
"boolean value indicating whether to IPI the specified CPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1146
msgid ""
"The function to run on all applicable CPUs. This must be fast and non-"
"blocking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1148
msgid "An arbitrary pointer to pass to both functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1151
msgid ""
"Target CPU selection and work queueing are done with preemption disabled. "
"This protects against CPUs going offline, but not against CPUs coming online "
"concurrently; newly online CPUs are not guaranteed to be seen or sent an "
"IPI. If **wait** is true, the final wait for remote completion happens after "
"that preemption-disabled section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1178
msgid "Force all cpus out of idle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1184 ../kernel/smp.c:1203
msgid "``void``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1
msgid "no arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1179
msgid ""
"Used to synchronize the update of pm_idle function pointer. It's called "
"after the pointer is updated and returns after the dummy callback function "
"has been executed on all cpus. The execution of the function can only happen "
"on the remote cpus after they have left the idle function which had been "
"called via pm_idle function pointer. So it's guaranteed that nothing uses "
"the previous pointer anymore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1197
msgid ""
"break all cpus out of idle wake_up_all_idle_cpus try to break all cpus which "
"is in idle state even including idle polling cpus, for non-idle cpus, we "
"will do nothing for them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1274
msgid "Call a function on a specific CPU and wait for it to return."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1280
msgid "``unsigned int cpu``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1278
msgid "``int (*func)(void *)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1277
msgid "The function to run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1279
msgid "``void *par``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1278
msgid "An arbitrary pointer parameter for **func**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1280
msgid "``bool phys``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1279
msgid ""
"If **true**, force to run on physical **cpu**. See :c:type:`struct "
"smp_call_on_cpu_struct <smp_call_on_cpu_struct>` for more info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core-api/SMP:10: ../kernel/smp.c:1282
msgid ""
"``-ENXIO`` if the **cpu** is invalid; otherwise the return value from "
"**func**."
msgstr ""
